From 05212ef5fc27ee9ad4e09b25f79a4c86fa101922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lvdi <l00993886@china.huawei.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:57:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(engine): use None attention_mask for packed sequences to
 enable block-diagonal causal mask

The non-Qwen3 path in _prepare_mb_list set attention_mask to
dict(full_attention=None, sliding_attention=None).  Qwen2Model.forward
checks isinstance(attention_mask, dict) and, when True, skips
create_causal_mask entirely -- so eager_attention_forward receives None
and applies no mask at all.  In a packed sequence this means every token
attends to every other token across sequence boundaries, making the
training forward compute global attention instead of causal attention.

This was the root cause of the TIM (Training-Inference Mismatch):
  - Jaccard (trainer top-k vs vLLM top-k): 0.093 (almost no overlap)
  - TIM |delta_logp|: 6.72 nats (94% spike rate)
  - Trainer argmax concentrated 77% on a single token

A/B/C/D control experiments confirmed:
  - dict(None) bug:        Jaccard=0.126, TIM=4.71, spike=77%
  - attn=None (this fix): Jaccard=0.605, TIM=0.68, spike=9.8%
  attn=None lets transformers auto-detect the packed format from
  position_ids (which reset to 0 at each sequence boundary via
  amend_position_ids + pack_tensor_dict) and build a correct
  block-diagonal causal mask via find_packed_sequence_indices.

After this fix TIM drops from ~6.7 to ~0.68 (the bf16 numerical noise
floor, consistent with B2 tri-ref HF-vs-vLLM |delta|=0.49).

diff --git a/areal/engine/fsdp_engine.py b/areal/engine/fsdp_engine.py
index 441aedd..05faeb1 100644
--- a/areal/engine/fsdp_engine.py
+++ b/areal/engine/fsdp_engine.py
@@ -1957,10 +1957,17 @@ class FSDPEngine(TrainEngine):
                 mb["attention_mask"] = None
                 padded_mb["attention_mask"] = None
             else:
-                mb["attention_mask"] = dict(full_attention=None, sliding_attention=None)
-                padded_mb["attention_mask"] = dict(
-                    full_attention=None, sliding_attention=None
-                )
+                # Pass None so that the HF model's create_causal_mask auto-detects
+                # packed sequences from position_ids (which reset to 0 at each sequence
+                # boundary via amend_position_ids) and builds a correct block-diagonal
+                # causal mask.  Using dict(full_attention=None, ...) here bypasses the
+                # mask creation path in Qwen2Model.forward (isinstance check on dict),
+                # which causes eager_attention_forward to receive None and skip the mask
+                # entirely -- making every token attend to every other token across
+                # sequence boundaries.  This was the root cause of the TIM
+                # (Training-Inference Mismatch) that broke Score Centering's tail model.
+                mb["attention_mask"] = None
+                padded_mb["attention_mask"] = None
             _prepare_multimodal_forward_inputs(mb, padded_mb)
         _drop_multimodal_payloads(mb_list.data)
         return mb_list
-- 
